articles/CBMitAFBVV95cUxNRkxwNUdpSmVHRnVLS2wyU3JMM3ZMdzhZMlVnZG9RUm9iUFBubVRoRGhkanpfOTJyMzQxVnpJY3ZHc183a3F1ZWZ3Mnp1UTdMLTVPM0NrU3M2Q3luamkybXpHOU1WQlpxVzFtSlRJdkhQaUVxWU9xV1g2dG16WFBPMkQ2SmxFMlc2Wk0wZEM2SnF6R3hYMDdjc1I2MVFfLXZLMHVoMHFubWhNRTBKaHRwTnFidl8?oc=5"}, {"title": "Poll shows Georgia U.S. Senator Jon Ossoff leading challenger Mike Collins", "source": "WJCL", "published": "2026-09-14T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiigFBVV95cUxOc0FDZV9IZnpnTjNRbWlpRWhLcGhOaE11OGxaTFFOd3dYcElna2pVYkt0VkVfZVNBVzlwU0pCdDhxTXdXcVM3eDczYk9WUXFZdThmajUtcWhFQTIwN3kxQWtuMW9NemZnRG91NEFhWWU3VnBXZlBjcXVnd2JwbzhaTFZpRHp4cmlraHc?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 9.52, "prior_sd": 5.0, "poll_margin": 9.28, "poll_sd": 4.69, "poll_weight": 0.53, "fundamentals": {"margin": 10.83, "lean": -1.0, "environment": 7.38, "incumbency": 3.0, "money": 1.45}, "rating_margin": 8.65, "sigma_race": 4.8, "sigma_total": 5.68, "baseline_margin": 9.39, "analyst_adjustment": -0.89, "key_factors": ["Ossoff's consistent 7-10 point polling lead across pollsters of all leanings", "Massive fundraising edge: $42.6M on hand vs Collins' $2.1M", "Consensus Likely D expert ratings and markets pricing Ossoff at ~95%", "Republican-leaning environment partially offset by incumbency and money"], "rationale": "Polls from both Republican-leaning and neutral pollsters uniformly show Ossoff ahead by 6-11 points, and he holds an overwhelming financial advantage over Collins. Expert ratings cluster at Likely D and prediction markets price Ossoff near 95%, so a Likely D forecast with a mid-to-high single-digit margin fits the evidence.", "watch": "A late national environment shift toward Republicans or a surge of outside spending against Ossoff could narrow the race toward Lean D.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Jon Ossoff (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Georgia's Senate race pits first-term Democrat Jon Ossoff against Trump-endorsed Republican Mike Collins, who won his runoff in late September. Ossoff enters with a huge financial edge, holding $42.6 million to Collins' $2.1 million, and every recent poll shows him ahead by six to eleven points, including surveys from Republican-leaning pollsters. Expert raters overwhelmingly call the race Likely D, and prediction markets price Ossoff's chances around 95 percent.\n\nThe main question is whether the Republican-leaning national environment can close the gap. Senate GOP leadership has campaigned for Collins, but the NRSC chair has left Georgia off his list of top targets, suggesting limited party investment. Headlines describe the seat as appearing to slip from Republican reach, though the governor's race in the same state is a dead heat, hinting at ticket-splitting potential.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9499, "margin": 8.78}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9449, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9229, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9348, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9317, "margin": 8.5}]}